    <h2 class="pd-title">Commercial General Liability (CGL)</h2>
    <section class="pd-broker-note" aria-label="Insurance broker note">
      <div class="pd-broker-icon" aria-hidden="true">⚖</div>
      <div class="pd-broker-body">
        <span class="pd-broker-tag">From a licensed insurance broker</span>
        <p class="pd-broker-text">
          <strong>N2N Insurance Brokerage</strong> does not represent any single insurer — it <strong>independently represents the client</strong>
          as an FSS-registered broker (Reg. No. 2026-012201). We compare the wordings, rates and service of AIG · Chubb · DB · Hyundai · KB · Meritz
          to propose the <strong>cover and price best suited to your risk</strong>. Each insurer's full wording is provided at application and binding.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <div class="pd-tabs" role="tablist">
      <button class="pd-tab-btn active" data-tab="tab1" role="tab">Overview</button>
      <button class="pd-tab-btn" data-tab="tab2" role="tab">Cover</button>
      <button class="pd-tab-btn" data-tab="tab3" role="tab">How to apply</button>
    </div>

    <section id="tab1" class="pd-tab-pane active" role="tabpanel">
      <div class="pd-section"><h3>Overview</h3>
        <p>Commercial General Liability (CGL) is the most basic corporate liability cover — it indemnifies legal liability for
          third-party <strong>bodily injury or property damage</strong> arising from <strong>owning, occupying or managing business premises</strong>, or from business activities.</p>
        <p>It applies to all business premises — factories, offices, stores, hotels, venues — and is often a <strong>mandatory condition</strong> in lease and tenancy contracts.</p></div>
      <div class="pd-section"><h3>Key features</h3>
        <ul class="pd-feature-list">
          <li><span class="pd-num">01</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Broad liability base</strong>
            <p>Covers third-party bodily-injury and property-damage liability across premises ownership/use/management and business activities.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="pd-num">02</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Essential for tenants / occupants</strong>
            <p>A CGL certificate is often a contract condition for occupying large commercial facilities and malls.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="pd-num">03</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Defense costs within limit</strong>
            <p>Covers lawyer and expert costs for litigation and arbitration.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="pd-num">04</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Modular extension</strong>
            <p>Cover can be extended with modular endorsements — PL, sewage, employee injury, subcontractor liability.</p></div></li>
        </ul></div>
      <div class="pd-section"><h3>Who needs it</h3>
        <ul class="pd-feature-list">
          <li><span class="pd-num">01</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Manufacturing / distribution / logistics sites</strong>
            <p>Managing visitor-accident risk across factories, distribution centers and stores.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="pd-num">02</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Lodging / F&amp;B / services</strong>
            <p>Hotels, resorts, restaurants, cafés, salons and other high-footfall businesses.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="pd-num">03</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Building owners / landlords</strong>
            <p>Defect and management-liability risk as a building owner.</p></div></li>
          <li><span class="pd-num">04</span><div class="pd-ftext"><strong>Event / performance organizers</strong>
            <p>Facility-accident liability of one-off and recurring event organizers.</p></div></li>
        </ul></div>
    </section>
    <section id="tab2" class="pd-tab-pane" role="tabpanel">
      <div class="pd-section"><h3>Main losses covered</h3>
        <ul class="pd-bul">
          <li><strong>Bodily-injury liability</strong> when a visitor is hurt by a defect in the premises (building / equipment)</li>
          <li><strong>Property-damage liability</strong> to a third party from employee or equipment negligence during work</li>
          <li>Third-party harm arising in the course of business activities</li>
          <li>Defense costs for litigation and arbitration</li>
          <li>Emergency first-aid and loss-prevention costs</li>
        </ul></div>
      <div class="pd-section"><h3>Main endorsements</h3>
        <ul class="pd-bul">
          <li>Product Liability (PL) extension</li>
          <li>Management-defect (tenant / custodian) endorsement</li>
          <li>Employer's Liability (employee bodily injury) endorsement</li>
          <li>Subcontractor additional-insured endorsement</li>
          <li>Leased-building liability extension</li>
        </ul></div>
      <div class="pd-exclude"><h4>Main exclusions</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>Deliberate unlawful acts by the insured</li>
          <li>Liability aggravated by contract; warranty liability</li>
          <li>Accidents while operating cars, aircraft or vessels (separate insurance)</li>
          <li>Pollution (separate environmental liability)</li>
          <li>Damage to property owned or managed by the insured</li>
          <li>Nuclear, war, terrorism</li>
        </ul></div>
    </section>
    <section id="tab3" class="pd-tab-pane" role="tabpanel">
      <div class="pd-section"><h3>Conditions &amp; process</h3>
        <table class="pd-info-table">
          <tr><th>Period</th><td>1 year (Occurrence)</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Payment</th><td>Single (annual) or installment</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Insurers</th><td>Chubb · DB · Hyundai · KB · Meritz</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Channel</th><td>Individual consultation with our team (+82-10-5755-6465)</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Turnaround</th><td>3–5 business days</td></tr>
        </table></div>
      <div class="pd-section"><h3>What we need to quote</h3>
        <ul class="pd-bul">
          <li>Premises type, address, area, annual number of visitors</li>
          <li>Annual revenue / number of employees</li>
          <li>Liability-claim / accident history for the last 3–5 years</li>
          <li>Desired limit of indemnity and deductible</li>
          <li>Requirements (limit required by the landlord/occupant, additional insured, etc.)</li>
        </ul></div>
      <div class="pd-section"><h3>Other notes</h3>
        <ul class="pd-bul">
          <li>An Occurrence contract covers losses occurring during the period.</li>
          <li>Notify immediately on a loss, and consult the insurer before settling with the injured party.</li>
          <li>Separate risks such as PL, environmental and workers' compensation should be reviewed for additional cover.</li>
        </ul></div>
      <div class="pd-section"><h3>Cooling-off / duty of disclosure</h3>
        <ul class="pd-bul">
          <li>Cooling-off (cancellation) is available within 15 days of receiving the certificate (excluding professional financial consumers).</li>
          <li>If the duty to explain material matters is breached or a signature is missing, the contract may be cancelled within 3 months.</li>
          <li>Breach of the duty of disclosure may lead to cancellation or reduced indemnity.</li>
        </ul></div>
      <div class="pd-disclosure">
        <span class="deposit-protect">Depositor-protected product</span>
        <h3>Things to note</h3>
        <ul class="pd-bul">
          <li>This is non-life insurance promotional material; cover, exclusions and limits follow the <strong>policy wording and certificate</strong>.</li>
          <li><strong>Final premiums and terms are confirmed after the insurer's underwriting review.</strong></li>
          <li>We work with 6 AM Best A++–A rated insurers (AIG · Chubb · DB · Hyundai · KB · Meritz) and place each line with the insurer best suited to your risk — not merely the lowest price.</li>
          <li>Our brokerage fee is paid by the insurer and is not added to your premium (Article 98, Insurance Business Act).</li>
          <li>Full Korean statutory disclosures (depositor protection, fraud reporting, dispute resolution) are on the <a href="/products/liability-cgl.html">Korean page</a>.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

